  "kind": "new finite construction",
  "attribution_note": "Source packing by Alejandro Zarzuelo. Original source credit: soft-to-rigid method by Yohei Nakajima (2026); generalization to Archimedean, Catalan, prism and antiprism solids, basin-hopping search and certification developed with Claude (Anthropic) under Alejandro Zarzuelo's direction. Classical Cartesian grid composition is used. PingYou Ltd supplies this complete finite box assembly and its native certificate. PingYou Ltd supplies the subsequent coupled whole-block translation return.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "joint_complete_block_translation_return",
   "proof": "Complete source-block translation return\n\nStart with each of the ten reviewed complete native box-product controls.\nThe block label is the first three entries of its retained grid/source word.\nFor every block z introduce ONE vector u_z. Every owner a in that block has\ncenter c_a+u_z and keeps its original quaternion. Thus its actual internal\ngeometry is fixed throughout the ideal return. Remove the containing-box\nwalls from the optimization: those were sufficient construction devices,\nnot physical walls between the owners.\n\nFor each actual cross-block pair a,b retain a rational separating normal n\ncertified at the source control. Compute g_ab as an exact outward lower\nbound for min(n.X_b)-max(n.X_a) from their complete native vertices. Impose\nn.u_a-n.u_b <= g_ab. This is ONE simultaneous linear system over all blocks;\nseparately feasible pair motions are never combined. Each real host wall\nhas its own complete-owner support h_a: sign*u_z[k]-S/2 <= -h_a.\nMinimize the ONE host side S. No frame/angle variable exists.\n\nThe original u=0,S=S_source is a strict feasible control. The numerical LP\nendpoint is only a proposal. Rationalize its full shared variable vector,\nthen mix it with the original state using ONE exact lambda determined by\nevery retained wall/pair row. This restores strict shared compatibility\nwithout dilating or changing internal block geometry. Every point along\nthe resulting segment satisfies the same rows by convexity. Retain the\nuncontracted source, full rows, controller labels, endpoint and lambda.\nThe final binary64 centers and outward side are checked again natively;\ntheir tiny coordinate rounding is distinct from the exact translation law.\n\nCompare all ten full controls to fresh complete public/private thresholds\nfirst. Only then retain those literal prefixes for which the complete\ntranslated control itself predicts a strict threshold crossing; do not\nrun a blind prefix optimization sweep. A later deleted-controller return\nwould be a separately derived operation.\n",
